# Shared mechanics (DRY gate)

Before coding a feature, mechanic, or UI, run this gate. Fuller intent: `ARCHITECTURE.md` → Shared mechanics.

## Ask

1. Does boardgame.io or our shell already own this?
2. Has another game in the cabinet already done it?
3. Will future games reuse it (known pipeline counts)?
4. If reuse is real or imminent: lift into a shared helper, shell slot, catalogue flag, or genre kit first — then plug the game in.

## Where shared things live

| Kind | Prefer |
|---|---|
| Pure rules helpers | `src/games/shared/` or genre folder (e.g. deckbuilder) |
| Shell UI (scores, status, leaderboard) | `src/components/` + optional `GameMeta` / board props |
| Solo leaderboards | `server/scores/`, `src/lib/scores.ts` — any `gameId` |
| Catalogue capability flags | `src/lib/games.ts` |

## Do

- Second use (or a clear second use coming) creates the seam.
- Genre kits (deckbuilder zones, shop, draw/discard/exhaust, turn resources) before cloning Unmuted / Hogwarts / Agency.
- Shared UI that games configure or feed — not copy-paste status/score chrome.
- Keep bots in mind: shared enumerate-friendly helpers make genre bots adaptable.

## Do not

- Invent a parallel rules engine (see `ARCHITECTURE.md`).
- Hard-code one game's assumptions into the shell (Dominoes is not the architecture).
- Abstract every one-off quirk on first sight — one-off rules stay in `src/games/<id>/`.
- Reimplement leaderboard or score submission per solo game when the shared API fits.
